# SfxLab bench v1: layer id name type dur seed key=value... (dur 0 = endless) · range id param lo hi [note] · bind signal id|* param [lo hi] [rel] [steps=N | scale=<chord>]
# aqueous v1 — the notes are made by SUBTRACTION. One stream recording runs through four resonant bandpasses, one per chord tone
# (C4 E4 G4 Bb4; cutoff = ln(f/40)/ln(250), keyed so the key moves them), and each copy's level is its tone.* signal: the water
# whispers the note. The bed is the underwater rumble tuned to C2 (a partials clip: sines shifted, rumble untouched). The surface
# (the stream, open) rises with stir and its bubble rate follows the pen's speed. The reward that forms is the stream's own
# droplets as partials, gathered onto the chord as the ratios come in tune (coherence) and growing with the machine (stack).
# fit sharpens the bandpasses: the right reach makes the note ring clear. No oscillators anywhere in the searching mix.
bench 1
root 65.4064
layer bed aqueous/Aqueous_underwater_rumbling_00001 7 0.0000 5001 level=0.60000 attack=0.80000 release=1.20000 pitch=4.42000 cutoff=0.45000 echo=0.00000 reverb=0.20000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=1.00000 keyed=1 file=aqueous/Aqueous_underwater_rumbling_00001.ogg drive=0.10000
layer surface aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 5 0.0000 5002 level=0.00000 attack=0.60000 release=1.00000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=0.75000 reverb=0.25000 loop=1.00000 pitch_mode=1.00000 speed=1.00000 keyed=2 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg drive=0.12000
layer root aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 5 0.0000 5003 level=0.00000 attack=0.40000 release=0.80000 pitch=0.00000 filter=1.00000 cutoff=0.34020 resonance=0.88000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg drive=0.12000 phaser=1.00000
layer third aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 5 0.0000 5004 level=0.00000 attack=0.40000 release=0.80000 pitch=0.00000 filter=1.00000 cutoff=0.38200 resonance=0.88000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg drive=0.12000
layer fifth aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 5 0.0000 5005 level=0.00000 attack=0.40000 release=0.80000 pitch=0.00000 filter=1.00000 cutoff=0.41340 resonance=0.88000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg drive=0.12000 phaser=1.00000
layer seventh aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 5 0.0000 5006 level=0.00000 attack=0.40000 release=0.80000 pitch=0.00000 filter=1.00000 cutoff=0.44480 resonance=0.88000 reverb=0.30000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg drive=0.12000
layer droplets aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001 7 0.0000 5007 level=0.00000 attack=1.00000 release=1.50000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=1.00000 reverb=0.55000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=0.00000 gather=0.20000 chord=2.00000 root_shift=-5.00000 keyed=1 file=aqueous/Aqueous_stream_00001.ogg
layer thud aqueous/Aqueous_impact_splash_00001 5 5.0000 5008 level=0.30000 attack=0.00500 release=0.20000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=0.80000 keyed=2 on=lock file=aqueous/Aqueous_impact_splash_00001.ogg
layer drip aqueous/Aqueous_drip_00001 5 3.0000 5009 level=0.40000 attack=0.00200 release=0.10000 pitch=0.07000 cutoff=1.00000 keyed=1 on=accept file=aqueous/Aqueous_drip_00001.ogg
layer splash aqueous/Aqueous_splash_00002 5 6.0000 5010 level=0.30000 attack=0.00500 release=0.20000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=0.80000 keyed=2 on=unlock file=aqueous/Aqueous_splash_00002.ogg
range bed level 0.3 0.6 the underwater rumble at rest, stepping back with stir and as the machine fills
range bed cutoff 0.3 0.6 how deep under the surface: the orb's radius lifts it toward the light
range surface level 0 0.35 the stream in the open, in with stir; drive 0.12 soft-limits the droplet peaks (+12 dB of body)
range surface speed 0.8 1.4 bubble rate (keep-len stretch), the pen's speed
range root level 0 1 the root: the stream through a bandpass at C4 (drive 0.12 ahead of the filter: the stream is peaky, this is its compressor)
range root resonance 0.7 0.92 how clearly the water whispers the note: fit
range third level 0 0.9 E4
range fifth level 0 0.9 G4
range seventh level 0 0.7 Bb4
range droplets level 0 0.8 the stream's droplets as partials, sines only: grows with the machine
range droplets gather 0.2 1 pulled onto the chord as the ratios come in tune
bind stir bed level 0.6 0.4
bind stack bed level 0 -0.12 rel
bind orb.radius bed cutoff 0.3 0.6
bind stir surface level 0 0.35
bind orb.speed surface speed 0.8 1.4
bind orb.radius surface cutoff 0.55 1
bind tone.root root level 0 1
bind tone.third third level 0 0.9
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.9
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.7
bind fit root resonance 0.7 0.92
bind fit third resonance 0.7 0.92
bind fit fifth resonance 0.7 0.92
bind fit seventh resonance 0.7 0.92
bind orb.curl root ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.curl fifth ph_pos 0 1
bind stack droplets level 0 0.8
bind coherence droplets gather 0.2 1
bind radiance droplets reverb 0.4 0.9
note aqueous v1 (draft, 2026-09-27). The subtraction plan: four copies of the stream through resonant bandpasses at the chord tones, levels
note from tone.*, resonance from fit. Cutoff for a note f is ln(f/40)/ln(250): C4 0.3402, E4 0.3820, G4 0.4134, Bb4 0.4448 (C5 0.4657).
note The droplets layer is the same stream as partials, sines only, root shift -5 so its F4 estimate classifies against C: gather (coherence)
note pulls the droplet pings onto a C major chord. bubbling_00001 and the gulps, swish-whip and freezing splash live in the spell files.
note One-shots: deep impact splash on lock, drip (C4) on accept, rock splash on unlock.
